message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "lm-puf: Machine-learning modeling attacks against liquid-metal physical unclonable functions (LM-PUF)"
abstract: >-
  Code for evaluating the robustness of liquid-metal physical unclonable
  functions (LM-PUFs) against machine-learning modeling attacks. Classical
  (logistic regression), deep (MLP, 1-D CNN, Transformer) and generative (GAN)
  attackers are trained to map five temperature features to a 1024-bit
  response, and are swept over decoy-key and featureless-key ratios to quantify
  the digital-cloning resistance of the device.
